# AWS Cost Management User Guide

> The AWS Cost Management contains features that enables you to better plan your costs through budgeting and forecasting, and methods to optimize your pricing to reduce your AWS bill. The AWS Cost Management contains features that enables you to better plan your costs through budgeting and forecasting, and methods to optimize your pricing to reduce your AWS bill.

- [Quotas and restrictions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/management-limits.md)
- [Document history](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/doc-history.md)

## [Use AWS Billing and Cost Management for AWS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/what-is-costmanagement.md)

### [Getting started with AWS Cost Management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/billing-getting-started.md)

Provides the first steps on how to get started with the AWS Cost Management console.

- [Reviewing your bills and usage](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/step-3.md): Learn about other pages in the Billing and Cost Management console you can use to customize your features.
- [Setting up your AWS Cost Management features](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/step-4.md): Learn about other pages in the Cost Management console you can use to customize your features.
- [What do I do next?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/what-next.md): Learn more about Cloud Financial Management, including resources you can use if you want to learn more about or need help with any of the AWS Cost Management features.

### [Using the console home page](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/view-billing-dashboard.md)

A general overview of the Billing and Cost Management console dashboard page.

- [Knowing the differences between Billing and Cost Explorer data](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/differences-billing-data-cost-explorer-data.md): Understand how to interpret your Billing data and Cost Explorer data for your AWS account.
- [Understanding recommended action types](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/recommended-action-types.md): Recommended actions automatically identify and prioritize the most important actions you should take related to Billing and Cost Management, regarding budgets, payments, cost optimization, cost anomalies, IAM permissions, and tax settings.

### [Controlling cost management data access with Billing View](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/billing-view.md)

Billing View is a feature that helps you manage and control access to cost management data within your AWS environment.

- [Getting started with custom billing views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/billing-view-getting-started.md): Custom billing views in AWS Billing and Cost Management allow you to make cost management data accessible to accounts both inside and outside your organization.
- [Creating custom billing views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/create-custom-billing-views.md): Custom billing views allow you to grant accounts, both within and outside of your organization, specific, controlled access to cost management data.
- [Sharing custom billing views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/share-custom-billing-views.md): You can share custom billing views with accounts within and outside your organization.

### [Managing custom billing views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/manage-custom-billing-views.md)

As the creator of a custom billing view, you retain full control over the resource even after sharing it with other accounts.

- [Editing the filters of custom billing views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/edit-filters-custom-billing-views.md)
- [Editing the sources of custom billing views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/edit-sources-custom-billing-views.md)
- [Editing the tags of custom billing views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/edit-tags-custom-billing-views.md)
- [Deleting custom billing views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/delete-custom-billing-views.md): Deleting a custom billing view permanently removes access to the custom billing view for all users.
- [Managing shared access to custom billing views in your organization](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/manage-shared-access-custom-billing-views.md)
- [Understanding AWS managed billing views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/manage-shared-access-managed-billing-views.md): AWS managed billing views are created when you map accounts to Billing Conductor billing groups or use billing transfer.
- [Managing shared access to custom billing views outside of your organization](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/manage-external-shared-access-custom-billing-views.md)

### [Accessing data using custom billing views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/access-data-custom-billing-views.md)

- [Custom billing views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/access-data-custom.md): If your account has access to a custom billing view, you can access the cost management data defined in that custom billing view.
- [Using AWS managed views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/access-data-managed-views.md)
- [Viewing a Cost Explorer report using billing views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/access-data-cost-explorer-report.md): Cost Explorer provides two types of default reports: cost and usage reports and Reserved Instance reports.
- [Viewing and creating budgets using billing views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/access-data-budgets.md): AWS Budgets supports primary and custom billing views, allowing you to create and manage budgets based on filtered cost and usage data across multiple accounts within your organization.
- [Viewing and creating exports using billing views](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/access-data-exports.md): AWS Cost Management Data Export supports primary, billing group, and billing transfer views that help you generate detailed cost and usage reports.

### [Visualizing and analyzing cost and usage data using Dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/dashboards.md)

Learn how to create, customize, and share AWS Billing and Cost Management Dashboards to visualize your cost and usage data.

- [Getting started with dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/dashboards-getting-started.md): AWS Billing and Cost Management Dashboards are collections of widgets that visualize your cost and usage data.

### [Managed Dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/managed-dashboards.md)

Managed Dashboards are preconfigured, read-only dashboards authored and maintained by AWS that appear automatically in your dashboard list.

- [Available Managed Dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/managed-dashboards-available.md): Five Managed Dashboards are available, organized around three layers of cloud financial visibility.
- [Viewing Managed Dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/managed-dashboards-viewing.md): To view Managed Dashboards, navigate to the Billing and Cost Management console, choose Dashboards from the left navigation, and select the Managed tab to see only AWS-authored dashboards.
- [Limitations of Managed Dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/managed-dashboards-limitations.md): Managed Dashboards are read-only.
- [Building your custom dashboards from Managed Dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/managed-dashboards-building-custom.md): Although you cannot edit a Managed Dashboard, you can use one to build a custom dashboard that you own, in two ways.
- [Exporting Managed Dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/managed-dashboards-exporting.md): You can export Managed Dashboards using the same export options available for custom dashboards:
- [Creating custom dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/create-custom-dashboards.md): Dashboards help you visualize and monitor your AWS costs and usage data by combining multiple widgets into a single view.

### [Adding widgets to dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/add-widgets-to-dashboards.md)

Dashboards help you visualize data through widgets - configurable components that display your cost and usage information.

- [Customizing dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/customize-dashboards.md): After adding widgets, you can customize your dashboard layout and settings.
- [Understanding widget types](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/dashboard-widget-types.md): Dashboards help you monitor and analyze your AWS costs, usage, and resource commitments.
- [Exporting dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/export-dashboards.md): Dashboards provide flexible export options for offline analysis and sharing.

### [Scheduling email delivery of dashboard reports](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/schedule-dashboard-reports.md)

You can schedule automated email delivery of your dashboard reports to stakeholders on a recurring basis.

- [Execution role permissions for scheduled reports](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/schedule-dashboard-reports-permissions.md): When you create a scheduled report, you must provide an IAM execution role that grants AWS Billing and Cost Management permissions to generate and deliver reports on your behalf.
- [Creating a scheduled report](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/schedule-dashboard-reports-create.md): You can create a scheduled report for a dashboard to automatically generate and deliver PDF snapshots to your recipients on a recurring basis.
- [Understanding scheduled report emails](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/schedule-dashboard-reports-emails.md): When a scheduled report is generated, recipients receive an email notification containing:
- [Managing scheduled reports](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/schedule-dashboard-reports-manage.md): You can view, edit, disable, or delete your scheduled reports from the Dashboards list page.
- [Sharing dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/share-dashboards.md): You can share dashboards with accounts in your AWS Organization or with external accounts (using AWS Resource Access Manager).

### [Managing dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/manage-dashboards.md)

After creating and sharing dashboards, you'll need to manage them over time.

- [Editing dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/edit-dashboards.md): You can modify existing dashboards to keep them relevant and useful as your needs change.
- [Deleting dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/delete-dashboards.md): Deleting a dashboard permanently removes access to the dashboard for all users, including any accounts you've shared it with.
- [Duplicating dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/duplicate-dashboards.md): You might want to duplicate a dashboard when you need to create variations of existing dashboards.
- [Adding tags to dashboards](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/add-tags-to-dashboards.md): Tags help you identify, organize, and manage your dashboards by adding descriptive labels.

### [Analyzing your costs and usage with AWS Cost Explorer](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-what-is.md)

Use AWS Cost Explorer to view and analyze your costs and usage.

### [Enabling Cost Explorer](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-enable.md)

Enable Cost Explorer to receive cost data for the current month and the previous 13 months, and forecasted cost data for the next 12 months.

- [Controlling access to Cost Explorer](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-access.md): Learn about how to grant access to Cost Explorer and how to control that access using Cost Explorer preferences.
- [Getting started with Cost Explorer](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-getting-started.md): Access the Cost dashboard in Cost Explorer to view estimated costs, forecasted costs, cost trends, and more.

### [Exploring your data using Cost Explorer](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-exploring-data.md)

Use the Cost Explorer dashboard to view your Cost Explorer costs and explore your Cost Explorer trends.

### [Using the Cost Explorer chart](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-chart.md)

Understand best practices when working with the Cost Explorer API to programmatically query your cost and usage data.

### [Modifying your chart](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-modify.md)

Understand best practices when working with the Cost Explorer API to programmatically query your cost and usage data.

- [Filtering data](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-filtering.md): Use Cost Explorer to filter how you view your AWS costs, according to service, Availability Zone, member account, and more.
- [Choosing advanced options](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-advanced.md): Customize how you view your data in Cost Explorer to include or exclude specific types of data.
- [Reading the Cost Explorer data table](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-table.md): A data table follows each Cost Explorer chart.
- [Forecasting](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-forecast.md): You create a forecast by selecting a future time range for your report.
- [Asking questions about your costs using Amazon Q Developer](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-nlq.md): Learn how to ask questions about your AWS costs using suggested prompts or the Ask question button in Cost Explorer, powered by Amazon Q Developer.

### [Comparing your costs between time periods](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-cost-comparison.md)

Use the Cost Explorer dashboard to view your Cost Explorer costs and explore your Cost Explorer trends.

- [Understanding how a cost comparison works](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-understand-cost-comparison.md): You can use Cost Comparison to quickly understand your cloud spending by automatically identifying and unfolding the largest cost drivers driving the cost variations between two selected months.
- [Performing a cost comparison](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-perform-cost-comparison.md): You can compare costs between any two months within the last 13 months to identify and understand changes in your AWS spending.

### [Exploring more data for advanced cost analysis](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-advanced-cost-analysis.md)

Understand how you can use your Cost Explorer data by enabling the feature at monthly, daily, and hourly granularity.

- [Multi-year data at monthly granularity](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-multi-year-data.md): Understand how you can use your Cost Explorer data by enabling multi-year data at monthly granularity.

### [Granular data](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-granular-data.md)

Understand how you can use your Cost Explorer data by enabling data at daily and hourly granularity.

- [Resource-level data at daily granularity](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-resource-daily.md): Understand how you can use your Cost Explorer data by enabling resource-level data at daily granularity.
- [Cost and usage data at hourly granularity](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-services-hourly.md): Understand how you can use your Cost Explorer data by enabling data at hourly granularity.
- [EC2-Instances resource-level data at hourly granularity](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-ec2-hourly.md): Understand how you can use your Cost Explorer data by enabling EC2-Instances resource-level data at hourly granularity.

### [Understanding your estimated monthly usage summary](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-estimated-monthly-usage-summary.md)

Understand your estimated usage records count for your granular data preference selections.

- [Understanding Cost Explorer data threshold limits](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-data-threshold-limits.md): Understand your usage records for resource-level data at daily granularity and hourly granularity features.
- [Estimating cost for Cost Explorer hourly granularity](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-hourly-granularity.md): Understand the monthly cost of your hourly granularity data.

### [Configuring multi-year and granular data](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-configuring-data.md)

Understand how to enable multi-year data and granular data in Cost Explorer.

- [Controlling access using IAM](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-iam-access.md): Understand about the level of access required to view and edit your Cost Management preferences in order to enable multi-year and granular data.

### [Using the AWS Cost Explorer API](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-api.md)

Understand how to use the Cost Explorer API to programmatically query your cost and usage data.

- [Best practices for the AWS Cost Explorer API](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-api-best-practices.md): Understand best practices when working with the Cost Explorer API to programmatically query your cost and usage data.

### [Understanding your costs using Cost Explorer reports](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-reports.md)

Learn how to create a Cost Explorer report and save it to your report library.

- [Using the default Cost Explorer reports](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-default-reports.md): Learn how to use default Cost Explorer reports to create your own custom reports.
- [Creating a Cost Explorer report](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-custom-reports.md): Learn how to create a Cost Explorer report and save it to your report library.
- [Viewing a Cost Explorer report](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/view-saved-ce-reports.md): Learn how to view your saved Cost Explorer reports.
- [Editing a Cost Explorer report](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/edit-saved-ce-reports.md): Learn how to edit an existing saved Cost Explorer report.
- [Deleting a Cost Explorer report](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/delete-saved-ce-report.md): Learn how to delete a saved Cost Explorer report.
- [Saving your configuration](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-bookmarks.md): Learn how to save your Cost Explorer configuration with bookmarks or favorites.
- [Downloading the cost data CSV file](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-download-csv.md): Learn how to download detailed cost data to a CSV file.

### [Managing your costs with AWS Budgets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-managing-costs.md)

Track and take action on your AWS costs and usage with AWS Budgets.

- [Best practices for AWS Budgets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-best-practices.md): Follow these best practices in AWS Budgets, including recommendations for controlling access, using advanced options, and setting alerts.

### [Creating a budget](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-create.md)

Create a budget with AWS Budgets to track and take action on your AWS costs, usage, and Savings Plans coverage.

- [Using a budget template (simplified)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budget-templates.md): Learn how to create a budget using a simplified template in a single page workflow.

### [Customizing a budget (advanced)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/custom-budgets.md)

Learn how to create a budget using a customized 5-step workflow.

- [Creating a cost budget](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/create-cost-budget.md): Learn how to create a budget that's based on your costs.
- [Creating a usage budget](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/create-usage-budget.md): Learn how to create a budget that's based on your usage.
- [Creating a Savings Plans budget](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/create-savingsplans-budget.md): Learn how to create a budget that's specifically for Savings Plans utilization or coverage.
- [Creating a reservation budget](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/create-reservation-budget.md): Learn how to create a budget for RI utilization or coverage.
- [Budget methods](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budget-methods.md): Learn how to set the amount of your cost or usage budget using fixed, planned, or auto-adjusting budget methods.
- [Budget filters](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-create-filters.md): Understand the available budget filters based on your chosen budget type.
- [Viewing your budgets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-view.md): View and filter your budgets to understand how well your budget matches your past cost and usage.
- [Editing a budget](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-edit.md): Learn how to edit an existing budget.
- [Downloading a budget](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-export.md): Learn how to download a budget as a CSV file.
- [Copying a budget](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-copy.md): Copy a budget to a new budget and edit the new budget.
- [Deleting a budget](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-delete.md): Learn how to delete a budget along with the associated email and Amazon SNS notifications.

### [Configuring budget actions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-controls.md)

Configure cost savings actions to notify you about budget thresholds that are reached and actions that are taken in AWS Budgets.

- [Setting up a role for AWS Budgets to run budget actions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-action-role.md): Learn how to create a service role in order to use budget actions.
- [Configuring a budget action](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-action-configure.md): Learn how to configure a budget action after you have created a cost or usage budget.
- [Reviewing and approving your budget action](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-action-review.md): Learn the process to review and approve a budget action on the Budget details page.
- [Creating an Amazon SNS topic for budget notifications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-sns-policy.md): Create an Amazon SNS topic so that you can send budget notifications over SNS in AWS Billing and Cost Management.
- [Adding email recipients to a budget notification](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-email-recipients.md): Add and verify email recipients for AWS Budgets notifications.
- [Receiving budget alerts in chat applications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/sns-alert-chime.md): Use Amazon Q Developer to monitor your budget alerts in Amazon Chime, Microsoft Teams, and Slack.

### [Reporting your metrics with AWS Budgets Reports](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/reporting-cost-budget.md)

Configure a report to monitor the performance of your existing budgets on a daily, weekly, or monthly cadence.

- [Creating an AWS Budgets report](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/create-budget-report.md): Learn how to create an AWS Budgets report.
- [Editing an AWS Budgets report](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/edit-budget-report.md): Learn how to edit an AWS Budgets report.
- [Copying an AWS Budgets report](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/copy-budget-report.md): Learn how to copy an AWS Budgets report.
- [Deleting an AWS Budgets report](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/delete-budget-report.md): Learn how to delete an AWS Budgets report.

### [Detecting unusual spend with AWS Cost Anomaly Detection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/manage-ad.md)

Use AWS Cost Anomaly Detection to monitor your cost and usage and to detect any abnormal spends.

- [Setting up your anomaly detection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/settingup-ad.md): Get set up to use AWS Cost Anomaly Detection in AWS Billing and Cost Management by enabling Cost Explorer and managing access with IAM.
- [Controlling access for Cost Anomaly Detection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/accesscontrol-ad.md): Configure your resource-level and attribute-based access control with Cost Anomaly Detection
- [Getting started with AWS Cost Anomaly Detection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/getting-started-ad.md): Configure your anomaly monitors and alert preferences in Billing and Cost Management.
- [Transitioning from customer to AWS managed monitors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/transition-monitors.md): Transition from customer managed monitors to AWS managed monitors
- [Editing your alert preferences](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/edit-alert-pref.md): Edit your alerting preferences, such as recipients, frequency, and threshold, in the AWS Cost Management console at any time to match your notification needs.
- [Creating an Amazon SNS topic for anomaly notifications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ad-SNS.md): Create an Amazon SNS topic so that you can send notifications over Amazon SNS for anomaly detection in AWS Billing and Cost Management.
- [Receiving anomaly alerts in chat applications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/cad-alert-chime.md): Use Amazon Q Developer to receive your anomaly alerts in Amazon Chime and Slack.
- [Using EventBridge with Cost Anomaly Detection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/cad-eventbridge.md): AWS Cost Anomaly Detection is integrated with EventBridge, an event bus service that you can use to connect your applications with data from a variety of sources.
- [Using AWS User Notifications with Cost Anomaly Detection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/cad-user-notifications.md): You can use AWS User Notifications to set up delivery channels that notify you about Cost Anomaly Detection events.
- [Opting out of Cost Anomaly Detection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/opting-out-cad.md): Learn how to opt out of Cost Anomaly Detection if you no longer want to monitor your spend patterns for anomalies.
- [Investigating anomaly root causes with Amazon Q Developer](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/investigating-ad.md): Use Amazon Q Developer to investigate the root cause of detected cost anomalies, including what changed, when, where, who triggered the change, and why it happened.

### [Identifying opportunities with Cost Optimization Hub](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/cost-optimization-hub.md)

Cost Optimization Hub allows you to consolidate and prioritize cost optimization recommendations across your AWS accounts and AWS Regions, so that you can get the most out of your AWS spend.

### [Getting started with Cost Optimization Hub](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/coh-getting-started.md)

This is an overview of how to get started with Cost Optimization Hub

- [AWS Organizations trusted access](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/coh-trusted-access.md): When you opt in using your organization's management account and include all member accounts within the organization, trusted access for Cost Optimization Hub is automatically enabled in your organization account.
- [Delegating an administrator account](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/coh-delegated-admin.md): You can delegate a member account in your organization as an administrator for Cost Optimization Hub.
- [Customizing your Cost Optimization Hub preferences](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/coh-preferences.md): This is an overview of how to customize your Cost Optimization Hub preferences.

### [Viewing your cost optimization opportunities](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/coh-view-opportunities.md)

This is an overview of how to view your cost optimization opportunities.

- [Viewing the dashboard](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/coh-dashboard.md): Learn how to use the Cost Optimization Hub dashboard to view your cost optimization opportunities.
- [Understanding your cost efficiency metric](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/coh-cost-efficiency.md): This is an overview of your cost efficiency metric.
- [Prioritizing your cost optimization opportunities](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/coh-prioritize-opportunities.md): This is an overview of how to prioritize your cost optimization opportunities.
- [Understanding cost optimization strategies](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/coh-optimization-strategies.md): This is an overview of the types of cost optimization recommendations.

### [Viewing your savings opportunities](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/coh-savings-opportunities.md)

This is an overview of savings opportunities.

- [Viewing recommended actions and estimated savings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/coh-view-recommendations.md): View a recommended action and estimated savings for a specific resource.
- [Grouping related recommendations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/coh-group-recommendations.md): Group related recommendations to view their estimated savings.
- [Exporting your recommendations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/coh-export-recommendations.md): Export your recommendations and their estimated savings as a CSV file.
- [Estimating monthly savings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/coh-estimated-monthly-savings.md): Learn about how to use estimated monthly savings as a quick approximation of future savings.

### [Optimizing your cost with rightsizing recommendations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-rightsizing.md)

While you can use the rightsizing recommendations feature in Cost Explorer to identify cost-saving opportunities, we recommend that you use Cost Optimization Hub to identify cost optimization opportunities.

- [Getting started with rightsizing recommendations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/rr-getting-started.md): While you can use the rightsizing recommendations feature in Cost Explorer to identify cost-saving opportunities, we recommend that you use Cost Optimization Hub to identify cost optimization opportunities.
- [Using your rightsizing recommendations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/rr-use.md): While you can use the rightsizing recommendations feature in Cost Explorer to identify cost-saving opportunities, we recommend that you use Cost Optimization Hub to identify cost optimization opportunities.
- [Sharing your rightsizing recommendations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/csv-details.md): While you can use the rightsizing recommendations feature in Cost Explorer to identify cost-saving opportunities, we recommend that you use Cost Optimization Hub to identify cost optimization opportunities.
- [Understanding rightsizing recommendations calculations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/understanding-rr-calc.md): While you can use the rightsizing recommendations feature in Cost Explorer to identify cost-saving opportunities, we recommend that you use Cost Optimization Hub to identify cost optimization opportunities.
- [Understanding reservations in Cost Explorer](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-ris.md): Learn how Cost Explorer provides you with an overview of your current reservations, shows your utilization and coverage, and calculates recommendations that could save you money.
- [Accessing reservation recommendations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ri-recommendations.md): If you enable Cost Explorer, you automatically get Amazon EC2, Amazon RDS, ElastiCache, OpenSearch Service, Amazon Redshift, Amazon MemoryDB, and Amazon DynamoDB purchase recommendations that could help reduce your costs.

