## [Security](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/security.md)

- [Data protection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/data-protection.md): Learn how the AWS shared responsibility model applies to data protection in AWS Cost Management.

### [Identity and Access Management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/security-iam.md)

How to authenticate requests and manage access your AWS Cost Management resources.

- [Overview of managing access](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/control-access-billing.md): Control who has access to your billing and account information with the AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) service.
- [How AWS Cost Management works with IAM](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/security_iam_service-with-iam.md): AWS Cost Management integrates with the AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) service so that you can control who in your organization has access to specific pages on the AWS Cost Management console.
- [Identity-based policy examples](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/security_iam_id-based-policy-examples.md): By default, users and roles don't have permission to create or modify AWS Cost Management resources.
- [Using IAM policies for AWS Cost Management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/billing-permissions-ref.md): What can I do with my AWS billing account? Learn how to apply permissions to users and view account information, usage reports, and detailed billing reports.
- [AWS Cost Management policy examples](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/billing-example-policies.md): See some policy examples for AWS Cost Management console features.

### [Migrating access control](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/migrate-granularaccess-whatis.md)

How to migrate IAM actions to granular access control

- [How to use the affected policies tool](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/migrate-security-iam-tool.md): Learn how to use the affected policies tool to identify IAM policies and reference the IAM actions affected by this migration.
- [Cross-service confused deputy prevention](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/cross-service-confused-deputy-prevention.md): The confused deputy problem is a security issue where an entity that doesn't have permission to perform an action can coerce a more-privileged entity to perform the action.
- [Troubleshooting](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/security_iam_troubleshoot.md): Use the following information to help you diagnose and fix common issues that you might encounter when working with AWS Cost Management and IAM.

### [Using service-linked roles](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/cost-management-SLR.md)

A service-linked role is a type of service role that is linked to an AWS service.

- [Service-linked roles for Cost Optimization Hub](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/cost-optimization-hub-SLR.md): Cost Optimization Hub uses AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) service-linked roles.
- [Service-linked roles for split cost allocation data](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/split-cost-allocation-data-SLR.md): Split cost allocation data uses AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) service-linked roles.
- [Service-linked roles for Data Exports](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/data-exports-SLR.md): Data Exports uses AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) service-linked roles.
- [Service-linked roles for Budgets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/budgets-SLR.md): Budgets uses AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) service-linked roles.
- [Service-linked roles for user attributes for cost allocation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ubca-SLR.md): User attributes for cost allocation uses AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) service-linked roles.
- [AWS managed policies](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/security-iam-awsmanpol.md): Learn about AWS managed policies for AWS Billing and Cost Management and recent changes to those policies.

